  "description": "Design a library management system (Microsoft, Swiggy, Zepto): books versus physical copies, a copy state table, loan limits, fines by member type as a Strategy, and a reservation queue that notifies through an Observer, in Java, Python and C++14.",
  "hero": {
    "tag": "header",
    "attrs": {
      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"2\">Level 2 - Beginner</span>\n    <span class=\"time\">Read 50 min</span><span class=\"chip\">Build 90 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Machine coding case</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Rank 23 of the LLD question list</span>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Library Management</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">The classic first \"management system\" problem, asked by Microsoft, Swiggy and Zepto in recent rounds: books and their physical copies, members with loan limits, borrow, return, renew and reserve, fines that differ by member type, and a waiting list that hands a returned copy to the next person and tells them. You get the requirements, the class model, a copy state machine, the patterns and why (Strategy, Observer, a state table), running Java, Python and C++14 code, a 90-minute plan and the follow-ups interviewers ask.</p>\n"
  },
